orkflow its substantive explanation with changes and retain only a short scope note in generation. Explain immutable evidence storage where contexts consumes it, while keeping storage focused on its actual persistence paths and any useful contrast. Do not expand an unconnected helper merely because its implementation was supplied."}],"regenerationInstructions":"Regenerate all 13 seeds together, preserving their successful functional boundaries and distinctions among immutable content, live state, captured evidence and publication. Establish a clear purpose and abstraction level for each point; prioritize consequential relationships over inventories. Consolidate repeated mechanisms within seeds, designate primary explanations across points, and label handoffs with object and identity scope. Correct ambiguous nesting and stage boundaries, retain material conditions on guarantees, and distinguish local component behavior from application wiring. Downrank disconnected helpers and routine constants. Use subject-specific structures rather than a uniform template or branch count. Treat the supplied final refinements as evidence of presentation ambiguities to resolve, not as independently verified source facts; leave layout, peripheral counts and routing to later phases."}{"ascii":"Git Change Proposals
|-- [M] Push intake: PushIntegrationService -> PushSource + PushWorkflow + store
|   |-- Public boundary: connect, receive, get, generations
|   |   `-- Connection identity is immutable; connection and application must enable generation
|   |-- [C] receive(connectionId, event)
|   |   |-- Decode generic/artifacts event -> derive ID from connectionId + eventId
|   |   |-- Same ID + same event -> share pending execution or return stored generation
|   |   |   `-- Same ID + different event -> PUSH_EVENT_ID_CONFLICT
|   |   `-- Create generation once -> classify push
|   |       |-- Non-branch ref, deletion, or unchanged endpoint -> skipped
|   |       `-- GitPushSource.resolve -> no net tree change: skipped
|   |           `-- Net change -> workflow.start(pinned context, requestId = generation ID)
|   |               `-- Store run/proposal IDs; get refreshes a running generation from its run
|   `-- [M] GitPushSource exposes validateConnection + resolve; Git execution stays internal
|       |-- Find registered checkout whose repository identity matches
|       |-- Ensure before/after commits exist; fetch missing endpoints by SHA
|       |   `-- Reject unavailable commits, shallow clones, or more than 2000 discovered commits
|       `-- [D] Resolved push depends on pinned endpoints
